## Getting started

1. Add a `metadata.txt` to the plugin directory — QGIS requires it to load the plugin.
2. Deploy with pb_tool:
   ```
   pb_tool deploy
   ```
3. Enable the plugin in the QGIS Plugin Manager.
4. Click the **$TemplateMenuText** toolbar icon to open the dialog.

## Files

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `__init__.py` | Plugin entry point, registers the plugin with QGIS |
| `${TemplateModuleName}.py` | Main plugin class, toolbar action, dialog lifecycle |
| `${TemplateModuleName}_dialog.py` | Dialog class loaded from the `.ui` file |
| `${TemplateModuleName}_dialog_base.ui` | Qt Designer UI file — edit this to change the dialog layout |
| `icon.png` | Toolbar icon |

## Customising

- Open `${TemplateModuleName}_dialog_base.ui` in Qt Designer to modify the dialog.
- Add your logic to the `run()` method in `${TemplateModuleName}.py`.

